.TH ORGANIZE 1 "November 2026" "organize.sh 1.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
organize.sh \- sort files and folders into category folders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B organize.sh
[OPTIONS]
[DIRECTORY]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B organize.sh
sorts files in DIRECTORY (the current directory by default) into category
folders. It recognises TV episodes, series, movies, music, dates, duplicates,
and custom rules. Moves are logged so they can be undone. A failed run is
rolled back automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t,\ \-\-target " DIR"
Move files into DIR instead of organising in place.
.TP
.BR \-r,\ \-\-recursive
Include files from subdirectories.
.TP
.BR \-F,\ \-\-folders
Also move top-level subdirectories into Folders/.
.TP
.BR \-T,\ \-\-tv
Group episodes as Videos/Show/Season NN/.
.TP
.BR \-M,\ \-\-music
Group tracks as Audio/Artist/Album/.
.TP
.B \-\-smart
Recursively identify series, movies, images, documents and music.
.TP
.BR \-H,\ \-\-hidden
Include hidden files and directories.
.TP
.BR \-n,\ \-\-dry-run
Show planned changes without applying them.
.TP
.B \-\-explain
Print a reason for each move.
.TP
.BR \-\-plan " FILE"
Write planned actions to FILE during a dry run.
.TP
.BR \-\-apply-plan " FILE"
Apply a previously reviewed plan file.
.TP
.B \-\-confirm
Preview the plan, then select moves interactively (requires whiptail).
.TP
.BR \-u,\ \-\-undo " [N]"
Undo the Nth most recent run in DIRECTORY (default: 1).
.TP
.B \-\-undo-list
List the undo history for DIRECTORY.
.TP
.B \-\-by-date
Add YYYY/MM subfolders.
.TP
.B \-\-dedupe
Skip files identical to already organised files.
.TP
.BR \-\-duplicates " MODE"
Handling for duplicates: skip, delete, move, or trash.
.TP
.BR \-i,\ \-\-include " GLOB"
Only organise files matching GLOB (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-x,\ \-\-exclude " GLOB"
Skip files matching GLOB (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-min-size,\ \-\-max-size " SIZE"
Filter by file size (bytes or K/M/G suffix).
.TP
.BR \-\-older-than " DAYS"
Only organise files older than DAYS days.
.TP
.B \-\-rename
Normalise file names while moving.
.TP
.BR \-l,\ \-\-link
Leave a symlink at the original path.
.TP
.BR \-\-rules " FILE"
Load custom rules and aliases from FILE.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " FILE"
Load default options from FILE.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the summary as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-watch " [SEC]"
Organise repeatedly every SEC seconds (default 5).
.TP
.BR \-\-jobs " N"
Use N parallel workers for moves (default 1).
.TP
.BR \-\-schedule " TIMES[@DIR]"
Install daily cron jobs.
.TP
.B \-\-unschedule
Remove cron jobs for DIRECTORY.
.TP
.BR \-\-install-timer " TIMES[@DIR]"
Install systemd user timers.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall-timer
Remove systemd user timers for DIRECTORY.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Check dependencies.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/organize/config.conf
Default command-line options.
.TP
.I DIRECTORY/.organize.conf
Per-directory options; overrides the global config.
.TP
.I ~/.config/organize/rules.conf
Custom rules, categories and aliases. Rules accept optional
.RI [ size OP N ]
and
.RI [ age OP N ]
conditions and
.BR {year} ,
.B {month}
and
.B {ext}
placeholders in destinations.
.TP
.I DIRECTORY/.organize-log-*.log
Undo logs (NUL-delimited).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR mv (1),
.BR crontab (5),
.BR systemctl (1)
